# qwen3.5-64k:9b: the Hermes desktop agent's model (profile chip) = qwen3.5:9b with a 64k context, the context Hermes asks for
# (model.ollama_num_ctx 65536 in the chip profile), so the copy pinned by scripts/hermes/keep_models_warm.sh is the one Hermes uses.
#   ollama pull qwen3.5:9b
#   ollama create qwen3.5-64k:9b -f tools/ollama/qwen3.5-64k.Modelfile
#   ollama show qwen3.5-64k:9b --parameters      # num_ctx 65536
# The parameters below are copied from the model used on 2026-10-07 (`ollama show qwen3.5-64k:9b --modelfile`); its base was a
# local blob (sha256 dec52a44569a...), assumed to be the library tag qwen3.5:9b (not re-pulled to confirm).
FROM qwen3.5:9b
PARAMETER num_ctx 65536
PARAMETER temperature 1
PARAMETER top_p 0.95
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER presence_penalty 1.5
